      </p>
    )}
  </PageHero>

  <section class="band band--surface" aria-labelledby="install-title">
    <div class="container downloads__install">
      <SectionHead
        id="install-title"
        label="Install Core-Geth"
        title="How to download, install, and run the Core-Geth client"
        em="download, install, and run"
      >
        <p class="lede">
          Each block takes the build most machines need: the x86-64 archive on Linux, Apple Silicon
          on macOS, the published image for containers. The note under each block says what to
          change for another architecture. For the full version of any step, and the cases these
          blocks leave out, read <a href={DOCS.installation.href}>the installation guide</a> on
          docs.coregeth.com. Check an archive against its checksum and its build attestation before
          you run it: <a href="#verify">both commands</a> are at the foot of this page.
        </p>
        <p class="lede">
          {`Every download on this page is the latest ${RECOMMENDED_LINE} release. If you are replacing a `}
          <InlineCode text={EXPOSED_LINE} />
          {` node, the upgrade is a security action rather than housekeeping, and that node needs a new P2P key before it starts again: `}
          <a href={`#${UPGRADE_ANCHOR}`}>{`moving a ${EXPOSED_LINE} node`}</a>
          {` has the commands, and `}
          <a href="/security/">what the audits found</a>
          {` says which flaws each ${EXPOSED_LINE} release still carries.`}
